From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:32:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: Animeko-style progress notification with
 speed and progress
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unify the download notification with the HarmonyOS builds of Animeko
and Anikku so that the three apps read alike in the notification shade:

- title: "Downloading N chapters" (queued + active)
- text: "Download: <speed>/s · <progress>%" with a determinate progress bar
- expanded text additionally shows the current "<manga> - <chapter>"
  (omitted when "hide notification content" is enabled)

Speed comes from a new DownloadSpeedMeter (3 s sliding window) fed by
wrapping every page body with countingInto(); the downloader refreshes
the notification once a second so the numbers keep moving between page
completions, and the notifier drops updates for the same chapter that
arrive within 700 ms.

Rebased from the v0.20.4 series (0006): v0.21.0 already rate-limits the
progress notification (500 ms, under a lock, always posting the last page),
so the fork no longer keeps its own 700 ms limiter; the paused notification
is the upstream one (separate id) and only gets the shared text.
